  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Justice for All-PFE 2022 - 2025 Donor Consortium - Justice for All-PFE Consortium Support</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Justice for All-PFE 2022 - 2025 Donor Consortium</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Protection of Human and Democratic Rights, Promotion of Rule of Law &amp; Good Governance and Peace Building</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protection of Human and Democratic Rights, Promotion of Rule of Law &amp; Good Governance and Peace Building. Justice For All - Prison fellowship Ethiopia (JFA-PFE) is an NGO which started its activities in 1992, supporting prisoners in Ethiopia. The organisation has gradually widened its operations to include human rights, rule of law and capacity building and advocacy in the justice sector justice. Recently JFA-PFE also engaged in reconciliation and peace-building.&#xa0;Sweden has supported JFA-PFE since the mid 2000s. The current program, &quot;Justice 2022-2025, An Integrated Program on Protection of Human Rights, Strengthening of Rule of Law and Peace Building Process in Ethiopia&quot; is supported by Sweden, Norway, Netherlands and Austria. This program was developed from JFA&apos;s new strategic plan &quot;Creating the Future&quot; 2021-2025 that was completed and approved in July 2021.JFA submitted the proposal in March 2022 and after reviewing the document, extensive comments were given to the cooperation partner to re-work on the proposal as well as to present a more realistic budget. The revised proposal was submitted in July 2022. The donors, have since been engaging with the cooperation partner to clarify and respond to certain questions that arose during the appraisal process.The budget for 3,5 years (2022-2025) is approx. 7,7 MUSD: The Swedish contribution is set to 20 MSEK, with 5MSEK/year. Other donors have pledged the following: The Netherlands 400000EUR/year, Austria 500000Euro/year (starting in 2023) and Norway NOK 5M/year.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall goal of the project is: 

&quot;Contribution to  enhanced status of rights, rule of law, peace building process and improved justice system in Ethiopia through advocacy, quiet lobby and capacity building trainings for the three branches of the government&quot;

The following three strategic objectives and results shall be realized to fulfil the overall goal of the project:

Strategic Objective 1: Strengthen Rule of Law in Ethiopia through improved institutional capacity of the justice sector to enact laws, policies, and create better access to Justice and improved Leadership capacity of justice sector.

Strategic Objective 2: Strengthen promotion of Human Rights in Ethiopia through enhanced capacity of the legislative, executive &amp; judiciary and media to respect and protect fulfilment of rights.

Strategic Objective 3: Support peace building in Ethiopia through enhanced capacity of stakeholders in peace building process, Traditional Peace Building Practices and Inclusive dialogue in Ethiopia.</narrative>
  </description>
